      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sylvester is a town in Boone County, West Virginia, situated along the Big Coal River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvester%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sylvester was incorporated on April 11, 1952, and bears the name of a family of settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvester%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before Sylvester was settled, the area hosted the Coal River Golf Club, featuring a nine-hole course and swimming facilities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvester%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A local businessman laid out the site for residential development after World War Two, calling it the Branham Addition of Whitesville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvester%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Sylvester was one of the first communities in the area not originally part of a coal camp, though it was settled by miners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
